msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:7
#: 241a3ce4b4bd49639a7a8a69b6ad54d1
msgid "This page describes how a Rover's speed and throttle controls can be tuned. In general it is best to tune this controller before moving on to the steering controllers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:14
#: dda6f779e9bc4378b1eb6ad166248359
msgid "Controller Diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:18
#: e58668028b53458e92887eed42bad3ca
msgid "Cruise Throttle and Cruise Speed (Throttle Baseline)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:20
#: 52471c37bc6046a6aae1e365407d6d54
msgid "The :ref:`CRUISE_THROTTLE <CRUISE_THROTTLE>` and :ref:`CRUISE_SPEED <CRUISE_SPEED>` parameters set the baseline throttle output used by the Desired-Speed-to-Throttle controller.  It is important that these two values are reasonable and consistent with each other meaning that the :ref:`CRUISE_THROTTLE <CRUISE_THROTTLE>` value (expressed as a percentage) should be close to the throttle required to achieve the :ref:`CRUISE_SPEED <CRUISE_SPEED>` (expressed in m/s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:22
#: 1f943e7f356f4658beee2e3b793c8d14
msgid "The easiest way to set these parameters is to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:24
#: 1efc268b28b44a5c93581b1520342fa9
msgid "Set the :ref:`Auxiliary Function Switch <common-auxiliary-functions>` to \"Learn Cruise Speed\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:25
#: 19cfc52d8eb94f95b4eef89b617adb2a
msgid "Arm the vehicle and switch to :ref:`Manual <manual-mode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:26
#: 12a627a9f7e646d88a004c9e8ca9bf77
msgid "Drive the vehicle at between 50% and 80% throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:27
#: bca7ff021b1a4e189c6e01fe45a36eed
msgid "Move the aux function switch to the high position for a few seconds and then back down to the low position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:28
#: b924a61454f14c50a928277a15db14ea
msgid "Check the ground station for a message like, \"Cruise Learned: Thr:XX Speed:YY\" which confirms :ref:`CRUISE_SPEED <CRUISE_SPEED>` and :ref:`CRUISE_THROTTLE <CRUISE_THROTTLE>` have been updated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:31
#: 3af69d2d3b96494ab36e89b2b85d6955
msgid "Desired Speed to Throttle PID Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:33
#: 6e909523ca894163b94c2f064daf1a55
msgid "The Desired-Speed-to-Throttle controller attempts to achieve the desired speed (set by the pilot or autopilot) using a PID controller.  All modes except :ref:`Hold <hold-mode>` and :ref:`Manual <manual-mode>` use this controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:35
#: fde72669899d44b8a1667574018c7b82
msgid "The P, I and D gains for this controller are held in :ref:`ATC_SPEED_P <ATC_SPEED_P>`, :ref:`ATC_SPEED_I <ATC_SPEED_I>` and :ref:`ATC_SPEED_D <ATC_SPEED_D>` parameters respectively.  :ref:`ATC_SPEED_FF <ATC_SPEED_FF>` should be left at zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:37
#: aecdf421087741e688b6ecde256095fb
msgid "Recommended steps for tuning this controller are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:39
#: d891a4a5f96a431f8a5bb3e017daa85f
msgid "Connect the ground station to the vehicle using a telemetry radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:40
#: 95321381dd39414cb2ee286af7059220
msgid "Set :ref:`GCS_PID_MASK <GCS_PID_MASK>` to 2 (Throttle) to send PID information to the ground station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:41
#: 7db1059a3fa84ea88f7fc40375dd46a6
msgid "On the ground station graph the \"piddesired\" and \"pidachieved\" values.  If using Mission Planner, Open the Flight Data screen, check the \"Tuning\" checkbox (bottom middle), double click on the graph and select \"pidachieved\", \"piddesired\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:46
#: d0b92f8a13e3469dbaefe2538a5b3a7f
msgid "Drive the vehicle at various speeds in Acro mode and compare how well pidachieved follows piddesired"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:47
#: 9844236e43754ab7821184e68c01ed3e
msgid "Adjust :ref:`ATC_SPEED_P <ATC_SPEED_P>`, :ref:`ATC_SPEED_I <ATC_SPEED_I>` up or down so that piddesired follows pidachieved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:48
#: f1cb1b7555f64c8e9ab8fd2aaf61b32d
msgid "The :ref:`P gain <ATC_SPEED_P>` is the most important and should be tuned first.  If the vehicle's speed is jerky and unstable then this parameter should be reduced.  If the vehicle is slow to get up to speed, this parameter should be increased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:49
#: 85f2cecd778a409d9ee232ab1e27b7a2
msgid "The :ref:`I gain <ATC_SPEED_I>` corrects for long-term error.  If the vehicle never achieves the desired speed, then this parameter should be increased.  If the vehicle's speed is slowly oscillating between too fast and too slow, this parameter should be reduced.  I should normally be lower than P."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:50
#: b34e865939ed4baa96fbf9ebddbf696b
msgid "The :ref:`D gain <ATC_SPEED_D>` is meant to stabilize the output by fighting against short-term changes in speed.  This can be left at zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:51
#: 877d79fe12e84c3586ef39e5157c3ffa
msgid "The :ref:`FF gain <ATC_SPEED_FF>` should be left at zero because the :ref:`CRUISE_THROTTLE <CRUISE_THROTTLE>` and :ref:`CRUISE_SPEED <CRUISE_SPEED>` are used to calculate a base throttle output which removes the need for feed-forward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:54
#: 23c60172e23f4447a5187b6136901446
msgid "Acceleration Limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:56
#: 0bab8fa5a6524891a9df29a5d1df1a1b
msgid "Although less important than other tuning values, the :ref:`ATC_ACCEL_MAX <ATC_ACCEL_MAX>` and :ref:`ATC_DECEL_MAX <ATC_DECEL_MAX>` parameters should be set to match the vehicle's physical limits.  This helps the speed controller avoid attempting impossible accelerations and reduces overshoot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:58
#: 6159c15555ad407bb5e7443524c1ec23
msgid "Use the ground station to view the forward-back (aka x-axis) accelerations in real-time.  If using Mission Planner open the Flight Data screen, check the \"Tuning\" checkbox (bottom middle), double click on the graph and select \"ax\". Note that the values are in cm/s/s so they should be divided by 100 to get m/s/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:63
#: 7da5498970c443d28895b2ddf4fd9a8a
msgid "Drive the vehicle in Manual mode, apply full throttle to accelerate from stopped to full speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:64
#: 7d32e40afc1745cdb407985477dd8eac
msgid "Use the displayed accelerations as a guide to set the :ref:`ATC_ACCEL_MAX <ATC_ACCEL_MAX>` and :ref:`ATC_DECEL_MAX <ATC_DECEL_MAX>` parameters.  Note that the values displayed may be in cm/s/s while the parameter is in m/s/s.  If the vehicles acceleration and deceleration are similar :ref:`ATC_DECEL_MAX <ATC_DECEL_MAX>` can be left as zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:65
#: 9c57760b20e8490587d55f160888da7a
msgid "Drive the vehicle in Acro mode to test the vehicle's accelerations are smooth and that decelerations are not too laggy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:68
#: af4a5d176167454eae9e5992da11e43b
msgid "Throttle Slew"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:70
#: 77dbfd99eed1413a9d08d74d58731a31
msgid "The :ref:`MOT_SLEWRATE <MOT_SLEWRATE>` parameter can be used to limit how quickly the throttle output can change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:72
#: 557db065b9894bd0927f02866f3221d4
msgid "a value of 100 allows the throttle output to change over its full range in one second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed.rst:73
#: c501a292f7fc472cb3bc15f3c7135450
msgid "a value of zero disables the limit"
msgstr ""

